.TH SDL_EnumeratePropertiesCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_EnumeratePropertiesCallback \- A callback used to enumerate all the properties in a group of properties.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_properties.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef void (SDLCALL *SDL_EnumeratePropertiesCallback)(void *userdata, SDL_PropertiesID props, const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This callback is called from
.BR SDL_EnumerateProperties (),
and is called once per property in the set\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
an app-defined pointer passed to the callback\[char46]
.TP
.I props
the
.BR SDL_PropertiesID
that is being enumerated\[char46]
.TP
.I name
the next property name in the enumeration\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY

.BR SDL_EnumerateProperties
holds a lock on
.BR props
during this callback\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_EnumerateProperties (3)
